{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/5/codegen_prompts/7.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed168776016/5`\n- 题号：`7`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed168776016/5/7.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"7\">\n- `description`：在网格的多个矩形窗口中，依据窗口边框上缺口的位置将窗口内的图案沿缺口方向推出，并用边框颜色填补推出后留下的空位。\n- `Input structure`：背景为 Black。网格中包含若干个由单一颜色（非 Black）绘制的矩形空心边框（宽度 1 像素）。每个边框的四条边中恰好有一条边上存在一个连续缺口（该段边框像素被移除为 Black）。边框内部包含一个由另一种颜色绘制的小型图案（不接触边框）。不同边框的颜色可以不同，内部图案的颜色也可以不同。\n- `Rule`：\n  1. 对每个边框，找到其缺口所在的边及缺口的位置。\n  2. 将边框内部的整个图案沿缺口方向平移，平移距离为图案边缘到缺口所在边的距离（即图案刚好移动到紧贴缺口边缘或穿过缺口）。\n  3. 图案被推出边框后，其原先占据的像素位置用该边框的颜色填充（相当于边框颜色向内扩展填补空缺）。\n  4. 被推出边框的图案部分正常绘制在边框外部（如果超出网格边界则裁剪）。\n  5. 边框自身（除缺口外）保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：解题者首先需要识别出缺口不是破损而是方向指示器——它指定了内部图案的推出方向。第二层推理在于填补规则：推出后的空位不是变为背景色，而是被边框颜色占据，这形成了一种\"边框吞噬内容\"的视觉效果，需要从多个样例中对比才能确认。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/a6f40cea, train/278e5215, train/6cbe9eb8, train/8a6d367c, eval/8b7bacbf, train/df9fd884, train/57edb29d, eval/4c3d4a41\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a6f40cea\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4172\nmechanism=0.5089\nlexical=0.0126\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:counter, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:rectangle, operation:bfs_distance, operation:count, operation:crop_resize, operation:translate, output:crop, relation:adjacent, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/a6f40cea.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/a6f40cea.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete partial paths inside a framed rectangle by projecting external color traces inward.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg, a 1px rectangular frame (border color) with uniform interior fill.\n- Colored components outside the frame touching its edges.\n\nRule:\n- Output = the frame's interior, filled with the fill color.\n- Map each outside component's frame-touch points into interior coordinates.\n- Monochrome components become solid Manhattan stripes between mapped endpoints.\n- Two-color components become alternating-color Manhattan paths.\n\nKey insight: Endpoint colors of two-color traces anchor the alternating phase deterministically.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"touch point s on closed rectangular frame where an open rectangular frame touches it\",\n  \"dst\": \"connect to another touch point d on closed rectangular frame where an open rectangular frame touches it\",\n  \"path\": \"path to complete the open rectangular frame\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"same color and pattern as the open rectangular frame\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to only retain inner area of the closed rectangular frame\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"278e5215\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3842\nmechanism=0.4142\nlexical=0.0128\ncode_feature=0.8333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:output_resize, object:hole, object:rectangle, operation:count, operation:crop_resize, operation:translate, output:crop, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/278e5215.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/278e5215.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor the large mask crop column-by-column using the separate three-row palette strip.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the most common color.\n- One large monochrome foreground object is the mask; its bbox is the output region and may contain background holes.\n- The remaining foreground is a 3-row palette rectangle with the same width as the mask bbox: two identical color rows and one uniform row.\n\nRule:\n- Crop to the mask object's bbox.\n- For each output column, color mask pixels with the corresponding color from the repeated palette rows.\n- Replace background holes inside the crop with the palette's uniform third-row color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe grey object is only a stencil; its columns select colors from the legend, while its holes expose the legend's fill color.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"palette column s in the separate 3-row strip\",\n  \"dst\": \"column d in the mask bbox crop\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.column == d.column_in_crop\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor mask pixels in d with s.repeated_row_color; fill background holes with the palette's uniform third-row color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"3-row palette strip maps each mask-crop column to its mask color; the uniform third row gives the hole color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to mask bbox\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6cbe9eb8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3742\nmechanism=0.4583\nlexical=0.0125\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:rectangle, operation:count, operation:crop_resize, operation:translate, output:crop, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6cbe9eb8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.\n\nInput structure\n- A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.\n- The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.\n- A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.\n\nRule\n- Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.\n- Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.\n- Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.\n\nKey insight\n- The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"foreground rectangular frames and solid rectangles over periodic wallpaper\",\n  \"dst\": \"nested lower-left inside the largest foreground rectangle\",\n  \"transform\": \"discard the wallpaper; sort rectangles by bbox area descending; rebuild each frame or solid rectangle, placing each next smaller rectangle at the lower-left of the current frame interior or solid bbox\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to the largest foreground rectangle bbox\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8a6d367c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3822\nmechanism=0.4701\nlexical=0.0127\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:hole, object:rectangle, operation:count, operation:crop_resize, operation:translate, output:crop, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8a6d367c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8a6d367c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\n- The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\n- The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\n\nRule:\n- Crop to the rectangular frame.\n- Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\n- Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"upper colored template mask s\",\n  \"dst\": \"rectangular frame interior d containing partial fill-color seed pixels\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"block-scaled s contains all seed pixels in d\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear dst to bg and paint the full matched scaled mask with the seed color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to the rectangular frame\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3577\nmechanism=0.4215\nlexical=0.0124\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:hole, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, operation:translate, relation:adjacent, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Find single pixels on grid edges that are endpoints of lines, trace along the line to find connected closed regions, and fill those regions with the edge pixel's color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"single colored pixels s on grid edge that are endpoints of a line\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed regions d connected to the line\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d is reachable by following the line from s\",\n  \"path\": \"trace along the continuous line from edge pixel s\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill interior of each closed region d encountered along path with s.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"d.interior.color = s.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify single pixels on grid edge; Step 2: trace the line connected to each edge pixel; Step 3: for each closed region touching the line, flood-fill its interior with edge pixel color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"edge-detection\",\n    \"region-filling\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"df9fd884\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3164\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"实现方案已经定下来了：\n\n1. 在 `main()` 里按颜色做 4 连通分量，筛出“像素只落在外接矩形边界上，且恰有一条边有连续缺口”的组件作为窗口边框。  \n2. 对每个窗口，从原始网格读取其内部图案坐标，按缺口朝向做单轴平移；先把原始图案位置染成边框色，再把平移后的图案画回去。  \n3. 在 `generate_input()` 里先为每个窗口随机生成本地 patch：方向、框尺寸、缺口位置、内部图案形状、颜色都随机，并保证图案 bbox 与缺口投影对齐。  \n4. 最后把多个 patch 无重叠地打包到全局网格，调用 `main()` 做一次自验，确保非退化、尺寸合法、输出与输入不同。"}}
